# Citation metadata for this repository and the technical report it accompanies.
# license: MIT covers this repository's own code and docs only; README.md, "License
# and third-party material", lists what it does not cover (measurement-db, the
# organisers' code, formative tables and inventory rows).
# version: the release tag (docs/release.md, sections 6, 10 and 11), not the Python
# package's version in pyproject.toml.
# keywords: the same list as the "Keywords:" line of docs/report/draft.md, which fills
# the PDF's metadata (tests/test_build_report_pdf.py checks they agree).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite the technical report below."
type: software
title: "Reading hidden runs at a benchmark-level cold start: a pair-rate oracle, test-like regimes and a calibrated hierarchical predictor"
abstract: >-
  Code, results and report source (report v2) for an entry to the Predictive AI
  Evaluation Competition (PAIEC) at NeurIPS 2026: a replica of the organisers'
  streaming evaluator; a reading of the hidden formative runs through a
  pair-rate oracle, whose score follows from the organisers' per-pair Brier and
  calibration tables; test-like regimes built from public data and checked
  against those runs; the submitted predictor, a hierarchical item-response
  model refitted from the revealed labels at every checkpoint, with a prior on
  a new benchmark's level calibrated on test-like runs tuned to the first
  formative run; a refit of its priors on the expanded public pool, which was
  not carried, under a rule committed and pushed before any scoring; and one
  script per reported number.
authors:
